>vanish in the old place...

There are three things that have to be done to run X-nethack. The
first thing is to tell the X-server where the font is. Number two is
to have a .nethackrc with OBJECTS and GRAPHICS for the nh10-font. The
third thing X-resources (it may work without them but not as good).

Another thing is that if you want to use the full potential of the
X-interface and have a colour workstation TEXTCOLOR should have been
defined when it was compiled (default is off, but there is no reason
not to have it defined), and set the option color...

>I'm on an decstation with ultrix 4.3 and the hints in the file
>x11-nethack from the nh313-release are not enough for me... 
>I installed the nh10.pcf (created with "bdftopcf -o nh10.pcf nh10.bdf")
>in a fontdirectory that is already in my fontpath.

Have you updated fonts.dir? It uses only the fonts that is specified
in that file! A new fonts.dir is created by mkfontdir (if you have
it), but if you have made it by hand you may have to patch it by hand.

The entries for the two fonts that is delivered with nethack is (on my machine):
ibm.pcf -misc-fixed-medium-r-normal-ibmpc-14-120-75-75-c-80-iso8859-1
nh10.pcf nh10

If you then copies the file win/X11/nethackrc to ~/.nethackrc (or
modifies your existing file) it will work. I dont know if you can have
a NETHACKOPTIONS, but they are better to have in .nethackrc anyway.

The last thing that need to be fixed is that nethack wants some
X-resources to be defined. There are several way of fixing this, the
best is to place the file win/X11/NetHack.ad as NetHack in the X
app-default directory. If you cant do this there are several other
ways of fixing this, the simplest is probably to insert it into your
own resources (it can be merged in using "xrdb -m NetHack.ad".


